/usr/local/bin/boss park fix/the-installer-builds-what-the-cargo-tomls-declare \
  --backlog-item fca10483 \
  --summary "The only from-scratch production-shaped installer now builds what the Cargo.tomls declare, and ships a UI. It hand-listed SEVEN binaries needing --features while the workspace declares 44 (measured from cargo metadata, 2026-08-29); cargo SKIPS a bin whose required-features are not enabled, so a fresh VM never built the other 37 at all and the install step copied whatever was left in target/release. Replaced by one call to infra/build-release.sh, which derives the set from required-features. It also never built the browser bundles — verify-replay.sh:191 has said 'API stack only' all along — so it now calls deploy-web.sh AFTER deploy-services.sh, which is what stages the generation deploy-web.sh rsyncs into." \
  --excludes "Does NOT fix infra/bootstrap-local.sh, which carries the same defect in a milder form: --workspace --features postgres plus two hand-named bins, which still misses the three gated on 'bin' and 'rebuild-bin' (boss-audit-integrity-check, boss-event-relay, boss-subjects-rebuild). Named here rather than swept in, because this packet is about bootstrap-vm.sh and a car that quietly grows to every file sharing a defect is a car nobody can review. Does NOT add a lint pinning 'every build path calls build-release.sh' — §9a prefers the collapse, and this collapses; a roster lint like schema-converge.sh's becomes worth writing when a path exists that CANNOT call it. Does NOT touch deploy-web.sh's behaviour: BUILD_AS becomes overridable and is byte-identical when unset, verified." \
  --test "bash -n on both changed scripts; the BUILD_AS override semantics exercised directly (set -> honoured, unset -> unchanged default). The 44-vs-7 count derived with the same cargo metadata + jq query build-release.sh uses, so the number and the fix share one source. NOT tested end to end: this is a fresh-VM installer and I did not stand up a VM — the change is a call-site swap to a script already used by the deploy path, and the risk is concentrated in argument shape rather than logic." \
  --verified "Gate green, read from packet 8242570b rather than the CLI line: receipt head=9f4ac833e7ebb8ac61094d20359f114f2de07221 matching the commit, mode=full."
